<title>HONG KONG: HK bourse deputy chief Herbert Hui to resign - paper.</title>
<headline>HK bourse deputy chief Herbert Hui to resign - paper.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Herbert Hui, deputy chief executive of the Stock Exchange of Hong Kong, has resigned after serving the local bourse for eight years, local newspapers reported on Friday.</p>
<p>A spokesman at the exchange declined to comment but said the stock exchange is due to release an announcement later today.</p>
<p>The exchange announced on Wednesday the appointment of Lawrence Fok as executive director, listing. Hui was head of the listing department.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6369</p>
